Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: TRANSPARENT PNG sprite atlas for tiny animals on a painted European fantasy board-game map.
Create exactly TWELVE isolated animal sprites in FOUR equal columns and THREE equal rows. One sprite or compact animal group in each cell, centered with generous empty alpha margins. Cohesive gouache / hand-painted storybook style, natural anatomy, viewed from a gently elevated three-quarter map perspective. Quiet cream wool, earthy browns, muted black/white coats, soft upper-left light; no heavy outline, cartoon faces or glossy toys. These are miniature distant map decorations, not animal portraits.
Exact row-major contents:
1 four cream sheep grazing loosely together;
2 five sheep with a small darker sheep in a compact flock;
3 three brown-and-white cows grazing as a small herd;
4 four varied brown and cream cows in a loose group;
5 one lone brown bear walking, full body;
6 one lone darker brown bear sniffing the ground, full body;
7 one red deer stag standing naturally, modest antlers, full body;
8 one lone doe grazing, full body;
9 one brown-and-white dairy cow grazing;
10 one black-and-white dairy cow standing;
11 one chestnut cow walking;
12 one pale cream cow grazing.
Groups must read as several separate tiny animals, with real space between their bodies; no overlapping muddle. Individuals should be simple enough to read at 12–18px and groups at 30–38px. Keep the same illustrated world as miniature farmhouses, forests and alpine map scenery. No people, fences, buildings, trees, scenic ground patches, labels, lettering or grid lines. No grass rectangle or opaque ground under feet. Genuine transparent alpha background in every empty space, soft natural edge antialiasing. DO NOT paint a checkerboard. Strict 4x3 atlas; no animal crosses a cell boundary.

Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: TRANSPARENT PNG atlas of tiny flying birds for a painted fantasy board-game map.
Exactly TWELVE separate SINGLE birds in FOUR columns and THREE rows. Every bird is airborne in MID-FLIGHT with spread or flapping wings, seen from above or a gentle top-down oblique angle as on a map; none standing, sitting, perched or swimming. Different but coherent silhouettes in one understated European storybook gouache style. These will render only 6–12 pixels wide, so favor clean recognizable wing/body silhouettes with a little soft painted detail, never huge portraits.
Row-major:
1 dark brown swallow gliding, wings swept back;
2 muted charcoal crow gliding with wide spread wings;
3 pale gull with grey wing tips banking left;
4 brown hawk circling with gently curved broad wings;
5 small dark swallow in downstroke;
6 tiny cream-and-grey bird in upstroke;
7 russet songbird in an oblique gliding pose;
8 pale grey gull banking right;
9 dark grey crow with raised wings;
10 tawny hawk seen straight from above;
11 cream bird with long swept wings;
12 small brown bird with one wing slightly lifted while banking.
Natural proportions, understated colours, no bold black cartoon outlines, no exaggerated eyes or beaks. Each bird fits comfortably in the middle of its own cell, occupying no more than half the cell width, with generous clear separation. Genuine transparent alpha background throughout all empty pixels; soft antialiased edges. No sky, clouds, backdrop, shadows on ground, checkerboard, scenery, text, grid or labels. Strict4x3 sprite atlas.
